    "chapter": "Fourier Transform and Fourier Series",
    "topic": "Fourier series",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n    <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n   \\[f(x) = \\dfrac{a_0}{2} + \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty (a_n \\cos nx + b_n \\sin nx)\\]\r\n<br/>\r\nIf f(x) is an even function, b$_n$ = 0\r\n\\[f(x) = \\dfrac{a_0}{2} + \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty a_n \\cos nx\\]\r\n<br/>\r\nIf f(x) is an odd function, a$_0$ = 0, a$_n$ = 0\r\n\\[f(x) = \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty b_n \\sin nx\\]\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/ff/Fourier_Series_sawtooth_approximation.gif\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fourier_Series_sawtooth_approximation.gif\">Jacopo Bertolotti</a>, CC0, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
