    "discipline": "Electrical and Computer",
    "subject": "Digital Systems",
    "chapter": "Logic Minimization",
    "topic": "SOP",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<ul>\r\n<li>The Sum-of-Products (SOP) form is a method (or form) of simplifying the Boolean expression of logic gates.</li>\r\n<li>Sum and product derived from the symbolic representations of the OR and AND functions.</li>\r\n<li>OR (+), AND(.), addition and multiplication\r\nf(A,B,C) = ABC + A'BC'</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nHere this is a sum of two product terms (ABC and (A'BC').",
