    "discipline": "Electrical and Computer",
    "subject": "Engineering Economics",
    "chapter": "Economic Analyses",
    "topic": "Cost-Benefit Analysis",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<h5><span><b>Benefit-to-Cost Ratios:</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<p><span class=\"math display\">\\[\\mathrm{Gross\\ B/C\\ ratio} = \\mathrm{\\dfrac{PV \\ of \\ benefits}{(PV \\ of \\ capital \\ costs + PV \\ of \\ operating \\ costs)}}\\]</span> <span class=\"math display\">\\[\\mathrm{Net\\ B/C\\ ratio = \\dfrac{(PV \\ of\\ benefits -PV\\ of \\ operating\\ costs)}{PV \\ of \\ capital \\ costs}}\\]</span></p>\r\n A project is economically attractive to be considered, if:\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$B - C \\geq 0, \\mathrm{\\ or\\ } \\dfrac{B}{C} \\geq 1$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 232</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n<h5><span><b>Steps in Cost-Benefit Analysis:</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Identify all projects or options that will be considered.</li>\r\n\t<li>Calculate net benefits for each one.</li>\r\n\t<li>Make decision.</li>\r\n</ul>",
    "important": "\\[B - C \\geq 0, \\mathrm{\\ or\\ } \\dfrac{B}{C} \\geq 1\\]",
    "resources": "",
    "images": [],
