    "subject": "Engineering Economics",
    "chapter": "Inflation",
    "topic": "Inflation",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class=\"container-fluid\">\r\n\t<div class=\"row align-items-start\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>The purchasing power of money declines when the prices increase.</li>\r\n\t<li>This must be included in equivalence calculations.</li>\r\n\t<li>A price index is the ratio of the price of a commodity or service at some point in time to the price at some earlier point.</li>\r\n\t<li>The Consumer Price Index (CPI) represents the change in prices of a “market basket,” that includes clothing, food, utilities, and transportation.</li>\r\n\t<li>The CPI measures the changes in retail prices to maintain a fixed standard of living for the “average” consumer.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nInflation adjusted interest rate is given by:\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$d = i + f + (i \\times f)$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 231</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\nwhere,<br/>\r\\ni = Interest rate per period<br/>\r\nf = General inflation rate per interest period<br/>\r\n\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n    \t\t<div class=\"col\">\r\n\r\n     <center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/05/World_inflation_rate_October_2024.png\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"></p><br/><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:World_inflation_rate_October_2024.png\">JJLiu112</a>, CC0, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n\r\n    \t\t</div>\r\n  \t</div>\r\n</div>",
    "important": "\\[d = i + f + (i \\times f)\\]",
    "resources": "",
