    "subject": "Engineering Economics",
    "chapter": "Risk Identification",
    "topic": "Risk Assessment",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-6\">\r\n   Risk can be formally calculated as:\r\n\\[\\mathrm{Risk} = \\dfrac{\\mathrm{Exposure}}{\\mathrm{Exposure\\ Limit}}\\]\r\n\r\nProcess for assessing risk:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Review the business model and strategy.</li>\r\n<li>Determine where desired and actual results diverge.</li>\r\n<li>Perform a risk analysis</li>\r\n<li>Identify the impact and frequency</li>\r\n<li>Create and put in place controls</li>\r\n<li>Reevaluate risk exposure and safeguards</li>\r\n<li>Report findings and communicate them.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6b/Risk-response.jpg\" alt=\"Risk response\" width=\"540\"><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Risk-response.jpg\">Nirjal stha</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
