    "discipline": "Electrical and Computer",
    "subject": "Ethics and Professional Practice",
    "chapter": "Intellectual Property",
    "topic": "Introduction to Intellectual Property",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class=\"container-fluid\">\r\n\t<div class=\"row align-items-start\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n\r\n<p>Intellectual property is an umbrella term covering patents, trademarks and copyrights. Intellectual property rights are specific abilities, granted by law to right holders, for the control of intellectual property. An intellectual property right is the legal right to property owned by a content creator and often protected through the use of a trademark or copyright.</p>\r\n\r\n<h5><span><b>Types of Intellectual Property:</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li>Copyright</li>\r\n\t<li>Rights in Performance</li>\r\n\t<li>The Law of Confidence</li>\r\n\t<li>Patents</li>\r\n\t<li>Designs</li>\r\n\t<li>Trade Marks</li>\r\n\t<li>Passing Off</li>\r\n\t<li>Trade Libel</li>\r\n\t<li>Cyber Law</li>\r\n\t<li>Broadcasting Rights</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n    \t\t<div class=\"col\">\r\n     <center><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1c/Intellectual_property_Noun_project.svg\" alt=\"Intellectual Property\" width=\"340\"><br/>\r\n\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Intellectual_property_Noun_project.svg\">Arthur Shlain</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0\">CC BY 3.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    \t\t</div>\r\n  \t</div>\r\n</div>",
    "important": "",
    "resources": "",
    "images": [],
    "local_images": []
