    "topic": "Theory of Complex Numbers",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-8\">\r\n\r\n<h5><span><b>Concept of Imaginary Numbers:</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<p><span class=\"math display\">\\[i = \\sqrt{-1}\\]</span></p>\r\nIf r is a positive real number, then:\r\n\\[\\sqrt{-r} = i \\sqrt{r}\\]\r\nFor example,\r\n\\[\\sqrt{-4} = i \\sqrt{4} = 2i\\]\r\n\r\n<h5><span><b>Complex Numbers:</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Complex numbers consists two parts, one is <b>real part</b> and the other is <b>imaginary part</b>.</li>\r\n<li>Complex numbers are represented as: a+bi, if b is zero, then the complex number reduces to only a, and now it is said to be pure real number. Alternatively, if a is zero , then it reduces to bi, and said to be a purely imaginary number.</li>\r\n<li>Complex numbers can be represented ona complex plane, where the real part is plotted along x-axis and imaginary part is plotted along y-axis.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b0/Simple_illustration_of_a_complex_number.svg\" alt=\"Simple illustration of a complex number\" width=\"340\"><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Simple_illustration_of_a_complex_number.svg\">User:Pengo, User:Oleg Alexandrov</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n\r\n<center><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/82/Complex_vector.jpg\" alt=\"Complex_vector\" width=\"340\"><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"<a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Complex_vector.jpg\">SiriusA</a>, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
    "important": "",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-s60PU13c5mUzH9aGXsAXHrXxQ48xS1g/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/40 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-200 transition-colors\">📄 Homework</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1TFTwLWCNL1ta03xi0caoXvxIKDQuHhHt/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-green-100 dark:bg-green-900/40 text-green-700 dark:text-green-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-green-200 transition-colors\">✅ Solution</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qpXSKCmd-clePTeBHfcUJENp3rU9f6wb/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a></div>",
