    "discipline": "Electrical and Computer",
    "subject": "Mathematics",
    "chapter": "Numerical Methods",
    "topic": "Trapezoidal Rule",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class=\"container-fluid\">\r\n\t<div class=\"row align-items-start\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\int_{a}^{b} f(x) dx \\approx \\dfrac{\\triangle x}{2}\\left ( y_{0} + 2y_{1} + 2y_{2} + 2y_{3} +.....+ 2y_{n-1} + y_{n}\\right)$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 61</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n<p>for n= 1 the above equation modifies to,</p>\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\int_{a}^{b} f(x) dx \\approx \\Delta x\\left | \\dfrac{f(a) + f(b)}{2} \\right|$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 61</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n<p>In trapezoidal rule, the steps are as follows:</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li>The area under the curve is divided into n intervals.</li>\r\n\t<li>The width of each interval is <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\Delta x = \\dfrac{b-a}{n}\\)</span> where a and b are limits of integration and n is no. of intervals.</li>\r\n\t<li>The area of each trapezoid is = <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)</span> <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\times\\)</span> <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\Delta\\)</span> x <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\times\\)</span> sum of parallel sides = <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)</span> <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\times\\)</span> <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\Delta\\)</span> x <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\times\\)</span> <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\left (f(x_{i-1}) + f(x_i)\\right)\\)</span></li>\r\n\t<li>If you add all such trapezoids, all vertical sides, except first and last one are added twice. The first and last vertical lines are added only once.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n    \t\t<div class=\"col\">\r\n     <div id =\"center\"><img src=\"https://onedrive.live.com/embed?resid=9C913AE725AFDEB1%21469&authkey=%21AAVoR6huPfe7f3M&width=340\" width=\"340\"/></div>\r\n    \t\t</div>\r\n  \t</div>\r\n</div>",
    "important": "\\[\\int_{a}^{b} f(x) dx \\approx \\dfrac{\\triangle x}{2}\\left ( y_{0} + 2y_{1} + 2y_{2} + 2y_{3} +.....+ 2y_{n-1} + y_{n}\\right)\\]",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RLf0471wxS9ZcdmGUpKsD_wRyLDw_DWC/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/40 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-200 transition-colors\">📄 Homework</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LBq0NvDiQO6bTws0I5tdgZqpfBoaj4rG/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-green-100 dark:bg-green-900/40 text-green-700 dark:text-green-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-green-200 transition-colors\">✅ Solution</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AmICpbY1uuCvWk9Edl7eCVoysxi9f0el/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a><!-- <div class=\"w-full mt-2\"><div style=\"padding:58.25% 0 0 0;position:relative;\"><iframe src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/580722323?h=d7f711ea41&amp;badge=0&amp;autopause=0&amp;player_id=0&amp;app_id=58479\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;\" title=\"Trapezoidal Rule\"></iframe></div><script src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/api/player.js\"></script></div> --></div>",
    "images": [],
    "local_images": [],
    "video": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LLiDR22M3aW5Djy4KBkxk1KHlViMmHdc/preview",
    "videoTitle": "Trapezoidal Rule"
