    "topic": "Routh Hurwitz Criterion",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n    <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n   <p>The Routh-Hurwitz criterion states that “the number of roots of the characteristic equation with positive real parts is equal to the number of changes in sign of the first column of the Routh array”.</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9d/Criterio_de_Routh_03.JPG\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Criterio_de_Routh_03.JPG\">José Antonio Torres</a>, <a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
