    "discipline": "Electrical and Computer",
    "subject": "Power Systems",
    "chapter": "Motors and Generators",
    "topic": "DC Motors",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-8\">\r\n   Armature voltage is given by:\r\n\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$V_a = K_a n \\phi$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 369</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\nMagnetic flux generated by the field current I$_f$ is:\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\phi = K_f I_f$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 369</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\nMechanical torque is given by:\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$T_m = \\left(\\dfrac{60}{2 \\pi}\\right) K_a \\phi I_a$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 369</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e7/DC_machine_cut_open.jpg\" style=\"width:340px;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DC_machine_cut_open.jpg\">Christian Kral</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\">CC BY 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
