    "discipline": "Electrical and Computer",
    "subject": "Properties of Materials",
    "chapter": "Semiconductor",
    "topic": "Tunneling",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>A severely doped p-n junction diode known as a tunnel diode is one in which the electric current drops as the voltage rises. In a tunnel diode, \"Tunneling\" is what generates the electric current. In computers, the tunnel diode is a highly quick switching component.  It is also utilized in high-frequency oscillators and amplifiers.</p>",
