    "discipline": "Electrical and Computer",
    "subject": "Software Engineering",
    "chapter": "Data Structures",
    "topic": "Arrays",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n    <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n   <p>An <b>Array</b> is a collection of homogeneous type of data elements.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>Advantages of Arrays:</b>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Convenient to declare</li>\r\n<li>Syntax is easy to code and remember</li>\r\n<li>Accessing by index number is faster.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<b>Disadvantages of Arrays:</b>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Size of an array is fixed and has to be speified at the compile time. Overallocation is often practiced to be on the safer side. This is not memory efficient.</li>\r\n<li>Insertion of new items is complicated at specific location, as it disrupts entire array.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3d/CPT-arrays-2d.svg\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CPT-arrays-2d.svg\">Pluke</a>, CC0, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
